From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:23:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] programs: build the host-arch services and conhost for
 arm64ec too

wine-11.20 (886f2ea) moved the choice of which architectures build a
module from configure into its Makefile.in (ENABLE_ARCHS). conhost,
lsass, plugplay, rpcss, services, spoolsv, termsv, winemenubuilder and
wuauserv are now built for the host architecture only, and winevdm for
the 16-bit one, so the arm64ec tree, which builds Playport's system32,
left them out, and the --enable-<program> options stages/wine-pe.sh
passes no longer choose architectures.

On iOS an x86-64 process cannot start a pure ARM64 one, so system32 has
arm64ec builds of Wine's programs (decision 0082); without conhost.exe
there a console program's conhost start fails again (c0000135). Add
arm64ec to these programs' ENABLE_ARCHS, which keeps the arm64ec set
what it was on wine-11.19. The aarch64 and i386 builds do not change.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-18-wine-11.20.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 programs/conhost/Makefile.in         | 2 +-
 programs/lsass/Makefile.in           | 2 +-
